  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThrough Friday: Continued hot and humid along with dry weather. \nLatest satellite imagery/RAP analysis showed the circulation around \na large and anomalously stout mid level high centered over southeast \nArkansas. This large high will shift a little farther west through \nFriday. Latest surface analysis had a >1022mb centered over the \nsouthern Appalachians that will continue to ridge back across our \nCWA through Friday. Together these features will maintain the well \nabove normal temperatures and dry weather across our CWA. Although \nnear record high temperatures are possible at Greenville and \nGreenwood again Friday, drier air from the east will continue to \nlower humidity and therefore help mitigate heat stress concerns. \nPeak heat index values Friday will approach 105F over the western \nand northern portions of the CWA with lower heat index values \nelsewhere. /22/\n\nHot and dry will be the story through pretty much the entire rest of \nthe period as the ridge remains dominant. This will tend to suppress \nconvection while maintaining hot conditions. Multiple days of a \nrecord breaking highs (99+) are likely, especially north of I-20 \ninto the Delta. Heat looks to peak on Saturday when the 850 thermal \naxis is maximized. A limited graphic will continue to be advertised \nthrough early next week. Despite highs in the upper 90s and low \n100s, mid 60s dewpoints will limit heat indices to around 100-105. \nIt is near heat advisory threshold however, so it is possible an \nelevated may be introduced should the need arise.\n\nA low pressure off the coast of Florida will be steered towards the \nNE Gulf and that will help to weaken the ridge for a few days mid \nnext week. Rain is likely to remain scarce, but this weakness does \nintroduce low rain chances by the middle of next week east of I-55. \nWe will also see decreased heat during this time. Thereafter, the \nridge restrengthens and heights increase once again across the \nregion mid to late next week. /SAS/",
